  "text": "Herd immunity functions similarly to a digital firewall in computer security. Just as a firewall protects a network by ensuring that enough computers are secured against malware, preventing an infected machine from spreading a virus to unprotected ones, herd immunity protects a population. When a sufficient number of people are immune to an infectious disease, the spread of the illness is halted, shielding those who are not immune.\n\nThe longest river in the world is the Nile River."
